body:
@cescoffier I see that `HttpClientOptions` (which is the what the REST Client populates via `org.jboss.resteasy.reactive.client.impl.ClientImpl`) has a `PoolOptions` object which we populate correctly.

However, `HttpClientBuilder` in addition to `HttpClientOptions` (which as we said, we populate correctly), can also be configured with `PoolOptions` (which we never do). 

What is the intended use of these two options? Should we copy the `PoolOptions` we are setting in `HttpClientOptions` into `HttpClientBuilder` with an explicit call?
